---
import BaseLayout from "../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetaPill from "../../../components/ui/MetaPill.astro";
import registry from "../../../data/phase-100-international-order-multilateral-cooperation-global-commons-cross-border-risk-shared-human-futures-registry.json";
const order = registry.international_order_diplomacy_treaties_international_law_peaceful_dispute_resolution_dossiers;
const multilateral = registry.multilateral_institutions_representation_development_cooperation_collective_delivery_ledgers;
const mobility = registry.migration_displacement_refugee_asylum_humanitarian_protection_shared_responsibility_registers;
const futures = registry.global_commons_transboundary_risk_catastrophic_risk_intergenerational_shared_human_futures_ledgers;
---

<BaseLayout title="International Order, Multilateral Cooperation, Global Commons, Cross-Border Risk And Shared Human Futures | FTFN" description="Thirty-two inactive international-order, multilateral-delivery, humanitarian-protection, global-commons, and shared-futures records.">
  <section class="page-section hero" data-international-order-multilateral-global-commons-shared-futures-registry><div class="hero__copy"><div class="eyebrow">FTFN / International Order And Shared Futures</div><h1 class="page-title">A treaty signed is not effective cooperation, and a global goal is not a secured shared future.</h1><p class="lede">Phase 100 traces diplomacy, treaties and international law; multilateral representation, finance and collective delivery; migration, displacement and humanitarian responsibility; then global commons, transboundary risk, catastrophic-risk governance and shared human futures.</p><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label="8 inactive international-order dossiers" tone="possibility" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive multilateral ledgers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive humanitarian registers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive shared-futures ledgers" /><MetaPill label="0 treaty or shared-futures decisions" tone="review" /></div></div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">International Order, Diplomacy And Treaty Implementation</div><h2>Eight international-order dossiers remain closed.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/treaties-ratification-domestic-implementation-compliance-001/">Read the treaty-implementation guide</a></div><div class="grid">{order.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.international_order_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/international-order-multilateral-cooperation-global-commons-cross-border-risk-shared-human-futures/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Authority, negotiation, treaties, implementation, compliance, dispute resolution, rights, distribution, review and receipts remain empty.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Multilateral Representation And Collective Delivery</div><h2>Eight multilateral ledgers contain no financed-delivery decision.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/development-cooperation-finance-additionality-local-ownership-delivery-001/">Read the collective-delivery guide</a></div><div class="grid">{multilateral.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.multilateral_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="22 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/international-order-multilateral-cooperation-global-commons-cross-border-risk-shared-human-futures/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.multilateral_institutions_representation_development_cooperation_collective_delivery_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Membership, influence, finance, additionality, ownership, capacity, delivery, evaluation, correction and remedy remain unassessed.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Migration, Displacement And Humanitarian Responsibility</div><h2>Eight humanitarian registers remain inactive.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/refugee-asylum-displacement-humanitarian-protection-responsibility-001/">Read the humanitarian-protection guide</a></div><div class="source-list">{mobility.map((record) => <article class="source-row"><div><h3><a href={'/evidence/international-order-multilateral-cooperation-global-commons-cross-border-risk-shared-human-futures/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.migration_displacement_refugee_asylum_humanitarian_protection_shared_responsibility_register_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Admission, asylum, reception, services, responsibility sharing, resettlement, return, reintegration and durable solutions remain unassessed.</p></div><MetaPill label={record.human_mobility_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Global Commons, Transboundary Risk And Shared Human Futures</div><h2>Eight shared-futures ledgers contain no stewardship or secured-future decision.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/future-generations-intergenerational-equity-shared-human-futures-001/">Read the shared-futures guide</a></div><div class="grid">{futures.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><h3><a href={'/evidence/international-order-multilateral-cooperation-global-commons-cross-border-risk-shared-human-futures/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.global_commons_transboundary_risk_catastrophic_risk_intergenerational_shared_human_futures_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Commons, boundaries, transboundary exposure, coordination, capacity, benefit sharing, catastrophic risk, future generations and remedy remain inactive.</p><MetaPill label={record.shared_futures_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band"><div class="briefing-band__copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Contract</div><h2>Inspect the empty international-order and shared-futures state.</h2><p>The export publishes the complete control surface without treating signatures as cooperation, membership as equal influence, commitments as financed delivery, data sharing as coordinated risk reduction, designations as stewardship, or global goals as secured futures—and without scoring or deciding for a person, community, state, institution, route, commons, region, generation or country.</p></div><article class="record-card"><a class="inline-link" href="/data/international-order-multilateral-cooperation-global-commons-cross-border-risk-shared-human-futures.json">International order and shared-futures JSON</a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
